# API contract (repo-a service `api`, internal only, no published port)

Base: http://api:8080  (container port 8080; UI service reaches it by name `api`)
Storage: SQLite file in a named volume, survives restart. JSON in/out, UTF-8.

GET  /health           -> 200 {"ok":true}
GET  /items            -> 200 {"version":<int>,"items":[{"id":<int>,"text":"milk","bought":false,"updated_at":"<iso>"}]}
                          ordered by id ascending. Version increases on every mutation (for polling/cheap diffing).
POST /items            body {"text":"milk"}            -> 201 {"id":1,"text":"milk","bought":false,"updated_at":"..."}
                          empty/whitespace text -> 400 {"error":"text required"}
PUT  /items/<id>       body {"text"?:string,"bought"?:bool} -> 200 item ; unknown id -> 404 {"error":"not found"}
DELETE /items/<id>     -> 204 ; unknown id -> 404
OPTIONS on any path    -> 204 with CORS headers (just in case)

Headers on every response: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS,
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type. UI must poll GET /items every 1-2s to see peer changes (<=5s requirement).
Basket-wide replace (optional, atomic, for future): PUT /items body {"items":[{"text":..,"bought":..}]} -> 200 {"version":..,"items":[..]}
Errors are always JSON {"error":"..."} .

